%SIXMD 1
# @?SED - APPLY A SMALL TEXT SUBSTITUTION

## @?OPTIONS

### @?-N - PRINT ONLY MATCHING RECORDS
SUPPRESS UNCHANGED RECORDS.

## @?OPERANDS

### @?EXPRESSION
ONE SUBSTITUTION EXPRESSION OF THE FORM S/OLD/NEW/ OR S/OLD/NEW/P.

### @?[FILE...]
S6REC TEXT FILES.  STANDARD INPUT IS USED WHEN NO FILE IS GIVEN.

## DESCRIPTION

SED IMPLEMENTS THE BOUNDED DAIMOSV1 SUBSTITUTION SUBSET.  IT REPLACES THE FIRST
LITERAL OCCURRENCE OF OLD IN EACH INPUT RECORD.  INPUT AND OUTPUT REMAIN NATIVE
S6REC TEXT; NO BYTE-TEXT FILE ABI IS USED.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - PROCESSING SUCCEEDED
### @?1 - INPUT OR OUTPUT FAILED
### @?2 - INVALID USAGE OR EXPRESSION

## @?SEE ALSO

### @?GREP
